    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-1 mt-2">
            <p>
                <b style="font-size: 22px">Subj:</b>
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-11 mt-2 ms-2">
            <span style="
    margin-left: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid black;
    font-size: 23px;
    font-weight: bold;">
                Intimation Letter – <span class="pcategory"></span> <span class="ptype"></span>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12 mt-2 mb-5" style="text-align:justify;">
            <ol style="padding-left:7px;">

    <!-- 1 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            The Management of N-Stack is pleased to inform that you have been allocated with a
                        <b><span class="ptype"></span></b> measuring <b>
                            <span class="pcategory"></span>
                            (<span class="psqryard"></span> Square Yards)
                        </b>
                        in N-Stack. Details of the plot as under:-
        </p>

        <!-- Inline Details Row -->
                    <table style="margin-top:10px;">
                        <tr>
                            <td><u><b>Phase: <span class="pphase"></span></b></u></td>
                            <td><u><b>Sector: <span class="psector"></span></b></u></td>
                            <td><u><b><span class="proptype"></span> No: <span class="ppropertyNo"></span></b></u></td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>
    </li>

    <!-- 2 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            <u><b>Payment Plan.</b></u> As per payment plan, you are required to deposit 
            <b><span class="pdownPaymentPercent"></span>%</b> Downpayment of Cost of Land by 
            <b><span class="ppdate"></span></b> while balance of 
            <b><span class="pbalancePercent"></span>%</b> will be paid in 
            <b><span class="pInstallments"></span> x</b> quarterly installments (Payment plan at Anx-A). 
            Development charges will be paid in 
            <b><span class="pdevInstallments"></span> x</b> quarterly installments (Payment plan at Anx-B) 
            after completion of Cost of Land.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 3 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            In case of failure, on the part of the applicant, to make payments within the prescribed period 
            or after Final Notice, the application/ allotment will stands cancelled. The amount deposited 
            by the applicant shall be refunded after the completion of the project. Refund will be made 
            after deduction of 20% of the amount deposited by the customer.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            A surcharge @@<span class="pSurcharge"></span>% per annum for delay of each day shall be levied 
            on the defaulted amount as per N-Stack by-laws.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 5 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            N-Stack reserves the right to make adjustment and relocate the plot, if need arises due to site 
            constraints or change in town planning. In view of escalation and other essential reasons, 
            additional development charges may be imposed, if necessary.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 6 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            Realtor will not be allowed to sell or transfer the plot before completion of construction.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 7 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            <u><b>Non Construction Penalty.</b></u> Will be imposed as per N-Stack Bylaws / policy.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 8 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            <u><b>Category Plot Charges.</b></u> In Case of Corner or park facing plot, 10% will be additionally charged. 
            However, if the plot is a corner as well as park facing, then 15% will be charged. The additional 
            amount 10% or 15% as the case may be, will be collected along with first installment of development charges. 
            Excess area charges will be collected at the time of possession according to per marla rate prevailing at that time.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 9 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            <u><b>Final Allotment Letter.</b></u> Final allotment letter will be issued after clearance of all outstanding 
            dues including sale consideration, development charges and applicable taxes/duties.
        </p>
    </li>

    <!-- 10 -->
    <li>
        <p style="font-size:21px;">
            We assure you of our best cooperation at all the times.
        </p>
    </li>

</ol>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
